Europe's General Affairs Council will  prepare this week for a summit of EU  leaders in March putting the spotlight  on climate change energy and the economy  the leaders are set to debate her  proposed framework for energy for the  2022 2030 period and to examine how much  has been done to implement energy  recommendations they handed down in May  at their meeting on the twentieth and  twenty-first of March heads of state and  government will assess progress that  member states have made in implementing  budget recommendations the  recommendations from the European  Commission a part of the so-called  European semester process which is aimed  at helping nations to strengthen their  budget and economic policies the leaders  are also likely to debate ways to  strengthen Europe's industrial base so  that it can help to spur economic growth  and create more jobs relations with  Africa and the EU Africa summit in April  are also on the agenda the General  Affairs Council will also appraise the  Greek presidencies priorities for its  term at the helm which include improving  civic and society engagement in the EU  reinforcing Europe's democratic  legitimacy and accountability and  deepening monetary union finally the  ministers will discuss a proposal to  authorize the cultivation of a  genetically modified type of maize the  council must pronounce itself on this  subject by the twelfth of februari
 

